WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.000
EPA 608 is not optional. You cannot legally touch refrigerant without it.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:30.000
ASHRAE Standard 15 is the Safety Standard for Refrigeration Systems. It governs
equipment room requirements, refrigerant detector placement, ventilation rates,
and emergency shutoffs.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:45.000
ASHRAE Standard 34 assigns safety group designations to refrigerants based on
toxicity and flammability. A equals lower toxicity. B equals higher toxicity. 1
equals no flame propagation. 2L equals mildly flammable. 2 equals flammable. 3

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:00.000
R-410A is A1. R-32 is A2L. R-290 propane is A3. R-123 is B1. Knowing these
classifications tells you what PPE, ventilation, and equipment is required.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:15.000
When you see a new refrigerant on a system nameplate, the ASHRAE 34 safety group
tells you immediately what precautions to take before you open anything.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:30.000
A2L refrigerants require A2L-rated equipment. You cannot retrofit. B-class
refrigerants like R-123 require more ventilation and PPE.

